faqs.a:
The following parts, sections, subsections, or appendices of the Model Traffic Code
               are inapplicable to this city and are therefore expressly deleted:
(a)
Part 1, TRAFFIC REGULATION - GENERALLY, Sections 101, 102, 104, 110.5, 111, 113, and
                  115;
(b)
Part 3, EMISSIONS INSPECTION, in its entirety;
(c)
Part 4, DIESEL INSPECTION PROGRAM, in its entirety;
(d)
Part 5, SIZE-WEIGHT-LOAD, Section 511.2;
(e)
Part 8, PEDESTRIANS, Section 804;
(f)
Part 12, PARKING, Section 1210;
(g)
Part 13, ALCOHOL AND DRUG OFFENSES, in its entirety;
(h)
Part 14, OTHER OFFENSES, Subsection (9) of section 1409;
(i)
Part 16, ACCIDENTS AND ACCIDENT REPORTS, in its entirety;
(j)
Part 17, PENALTIES AND PROCEDURES, Preface, sections 1701, 1702, 1703, 1704, 1706,
                  1707, 1708, 1709, 1710, 1711, 1712, 1713, 1714, 1715, 1716, and 1717;
(k)
Part 18, VEHICLES ABANDONED ON PUBLIC PROPERTY, in its entirety;
(l)
Part 19, SCHOOL BUS REQUIREMENTS, Sections 1901, 1902, and 1904;
(m)
All sections or subsections of the 2010 edition of the Model Traffic Code that categorize
                  violations into classes of traffic infractions, traffic offenses, or misdemeanors,
                  or which set forth a specific penalty for a violation, whether monetary or otherwise;
(n)
Appendix, Part A, Instructions for adopting the Model Traffic Code by reference;
(o)
Appendix, Part B, Specimen ordinance for adopting the Model Traffic Code by reference;
(p)
Appendix, Part C, Specimen notice of hearing;
(q)
Appendix, Part D, Specimen Certification - Posting of ordinance;
(r)
Appendix, Part E, Instructions for amending Model Traffic Code previously adopted
                  by reference;
(s)
Appendix, Part F, Listing of amendments for updating previous edition of Model Traffic
                  Code adopted by reference; and
(t)
Appendix, Part G, Specimen certification of Model Traffic Code.
(
Ord. No. 4384, § 2, 4-15-2013
)
